{"meta":{"format_version":"4.10","model_format":"free","box_uv":false},"name":"ballista","model_identifier":"ballista","visible_box":[1,1,0],"variable_placeholders":"","variable_placeholder_buttons":[],"timeline_setups":[],"unhandled_root_fields":{"description":"## ballista\n\nBallista (E4).\n\n- Cubes: 53 (17 rotated). Texture 256x256, 1 px per unit, embedded.\n- Bounds at rest: x -39.9..39.9, y 0.0..47.0, z -38.0..47.5 (size 79.8 x 47.0 x 85.5 u = 224 x 132 x 240 cm).\nBallista: a giant torsion crossbow (stock 2.2 m = 78 u; bow arms 78 u across cocked, 84 u = 2.4 m released) on a pivoting yoke on a post, fixed to a two-wheeled oak base with a trail to the ground, iron-tyred 0.8 m wheels and a team-colour stripe on both base beams. Twisted sinew skeins between iron-banded spring bars drive the two arms; a slider claw holds the string, a rear windlass with two cranks and a ratchet winds it back. Faces -Z. The rest pose is cocked (arms swept back 25 deg, string drawn to the claw).\n\n**Hit box:** one box 80 x 47 x 86 u (w x h x d), from y = 0, centred x = 0, z = 5.\n\n**Bones:** `root` > `base` (pivot at the trail shoe) > `turret` (pivot on top of the post, 37 u up: **yaw = Y, tilt = X**; the game can drive it directly to aim) > `arm_r` / `arm_l` (pivots in the skeins) > `string_r` / `string_l` (pivots at the arm tips), `slider` (claw + trigger), `winch`; `wheel_r` / `wheel_l` on `root`.\n\n**Slots:** `slot_bolt` on the turret at the claw (1.4 u back, 42.5 u up): put the `ballista_bolt` here with its nock at the slot, point toward -Z (spawn the flying bolt from it at the fire key); `slot_hitch` at the trail shoe; `slot_crew_1` behind-right at the windlass; `slot_crew_2` on the left beside the bow. Crew slots on the ground under `root`.\n\n**Move speed:** `move` designed for 35.6 u/s (1.0 m/s): one wheel turn per 2.47 s (circumference 88.0 u), travel toward -Z; `move_towed` rolls the other way (trail first).\n\n**Key times:** `fire` key 0.06 s (the bolt leaves: arms snap forward 0.04-0.10 s, the cords straighten, the turret kicks up 1.5 deg and the base jolts back 1.2 u). `fire` ends released (arms forward): play `reload` next. `reload` 3.6 s: the slider runs forward to catch the string (0.2-0.9 s), then the cranks turn 1.5 times in 6 ratchet steps while arms, cords and slider are drawn back; key 3.6 s (cocked, place a new bolt). `aim` loops yaw +/-35 deg with tilt -4..+6 deg. `damaged` 0.7 s shudder, the left wheel wobbles. `destroyed` holds: the right wheel breaks off flat, the base drops on its right side, the turret breaks off its yoke and slumps nose-first into the ground with the left arm snapped.\n\n| clip | length (s) | loop |\n|---|---|---|\n| `idle` | 4 | loop |\n| `move` | 2.471 | loop |\n| `move_towed` | 2.471 | loop |\n| `aim` | 4 | loop |\n| `fire` | 1.2 | once |\n| `reload` | 3.6 | once |\n| `damaged` | 0.7 | once |\n| `destroyed` | 2 | hold |\n"},"description":"## ballista\n\nBallista (E4).\n\n- Cubes: 53 (17 rotated). Texture 256x256, 1 px per unit, embedded.\n- Bounds at rest: x -39.9..39.9, y 0.0..47.0, z -38.0..47.5 (size 79.8 x 47.0 x 85.5 u = 224 x 132 x 240 cm).\nBallista: a giant torsion crossbow (stock 2.2 m = 78 u; bow arms 78 u across cocked, 84 u = 2.4 m released) on a pivoting yoke on a post, fixed to a two-wheeled oak base with a trail to the ground, iron-tyred 0.8 m wheels and a team-colour stripe on both base beams. Twisted sinew skeins between iron-banded spring bars drive the two arms; a slider claw holds the string, a rear windlass with two cranks and a ratchet winds it back. Faces -Z. The rest pose is cocked (arms swept back 25 deg, string drawn to the claw).\n\n**Hit box:** one box 80 x 47 x 86 u (w x h x d), from y = 0, centred x = 0, z = 5.\n\n**Bones:** `root` > `base` (pivot at the trail shoe) > `turret` (pivot on top of the post, 37 u up: **yaw = Y, tilt = X**; the game can drive it directly to aim) > `arm_r` / `arm_l` (pivots in the skeins) > `string_r` / `string_l` (pivots at the arm tips), `slider` (claw + trigger), `winch`; `wheel_r` / `wheel_l` on `root`.\n\n**Slots:** `slot_bolt` on the turret at the claw (1.4 u back, 42.5 u up): put the `ballista_bolt` here with its nock at the slot, point toward -Z (spawn the flying bolt from it at the fire key); `slot_hitch` at the trail shoe; `slot_crew_1` behind-right at the windlass; `slot_crew_2` on the left beside the bow. Crew slots on the ground under `root`.\n\n**Move speed:** `move` designed for 35.6 u/s (1.0 m/s): one wheel turn per 2.47 s (circumference 88.0 u), travel toward -Z; `move_towed` rolls the other way (trail first).\n\n**Key times:** `fire` key 0.06 s (the bolt leaves: arms snap forward 0.04-0.10 s, the cords straighten, the turret kicks up 1.5 deg and the base jolts back 1.2 u). `fire` ends released (arms forward): play `reload` next. `reload` 3.6 s: the slider runs forward to catch the string (0.2-0.9 s), then the cranks turn 1.5 times in 6 ratchet steps while arms, cords and slider are drawn back; key 3.6 s (cocked, place a new bolt). `aim` loops yaw +/-35 deg with tilt -4..+6 deg. `damaged` 0.7 s shudder, the left wheel wobbles. `destroyed` holds: the right wheel breaks off flat, the base drops on its right side, the turret breaks off its yoke and slumps nose-first into the ground with the left arm snapped.\n\n| clip | length (s) | loop |\n|---|---|---|\n| `idle` | 4 | loop |\n| `move` | 2.471 | loop |\n| `move_towed` | 2.471 | loop |\n| `aim` | 4 | loop |\n| `fire` | 1.2 | once |\n| `reload` | 3.6 | once |\n| `damaged` | 0.7 | once |\n| `destroyed` | 2 | hold |\n","resolution":{"width":256,"height":256},"elements":[{"name":"beam_r","box_uv":false,"rescale":false,"locked":false,"light_emission":0,"render_order":"default","allow_mirror_modeling":true,"from":[9.0,11.0,-18.0],"to":[12.5,16.0,20.0],"autouv":0,"color":0,"inflate":0.0,"origin":[0.0,0.0,46.0],"faces":{"north":{"uv":[224,87,227.5,92.0],"texture":0},"east":{"uv":[176,78,214.0,83.0],"texture":0},"south":{"uv":[228,87,231.5,